    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d912">

                <pb facs="1033" n="929" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg929"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00 Bandit Activities/469: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Honduras</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Higgins</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-07-12T18:00:00-04:00">July 12, 1932—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>29. Your 58, July 10, 9 a.m. In your discussion with the President you may omit
                    reference to the points mentioned in the last two sentences of the penultimate
                    paragraph of the Department’s instruction No. 305 of July 1.</p>
                <p>Department approves your suggestion as to the specific measures which you should
                    propose that the President carry out in an effort to improve the situation on
                    the frontier.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
